        "original_id": "87a64deb-9606-5d25-8f2a-8a5c5750f0a9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Moominpappa at Sea, The Old Man and the Sea, Moominvalley in November\n- People: Ernest Hemingway\n- Topics: titles, publication, chronology, Moomin family absence\n\nFacts:\n- In 1951, Ernest Hemingway wrote The Old Man and the Sea in Bimini, Bahamas.\n- In 1952, The Old Man and the Sea was published as a short novel by American author Ernest Hemingway.\n- In 1965, Moominpappa at Sea was published before Moominvalley in November and is contemporaneous with it.\n- The original title of Moominpappa at Sea is a loose reference to Ernest Hemingway's The Old Man and the Sea.\n- The translation of Moominpappa at Sea does not reflect the original title's reference to The Old Man and the Sea.\n- Moominvalley in November is the only installment in its series in which the titular Moomin family are absent.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4775cedf-f0d6-505a-9880-2638d9886720",
        "text": "Page: Moominpappa at Sea. Sentence: The original title is a loose reference to Hemingway novel \"The Old Man and the Sea\", though this is not reflected in the translation.\nPage: The Old Man and the Sea. Sentence: The Old Man and the Sea is a short novel written by the American author Ernest Hemingway in 1951 in Bimini, Bahamas, and published in 1952.\nPage: Moominvalley in November. Sentence: Set contemporaneously with her previous novel \"Moominpappa at Sea\" (1965), it is the only installment in the series where the titular Moomin family are actually absent.",
